From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Orchard migration <noreply@orchardlinux>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:31:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: msgbuf: Map RX buffers for device reads too

RX buffers posted to a PCIe dongle are mapped DMA_FROM_DEVICE, so an IOMMU
that enforces access permissions gives the device write-only access. The
BCM4355C1 firmware in the iPad 6 also reads posted RX buffers during
association. Behind Apple's DART each read is a READ FAULT, at every
EAPOL retry, and the firmware then stops answering control messages.
Association never completes, and scans and ioctls time out.

Map RX buffers DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL; map and unmap both take the direction
from the pktid pool. Without an IOMMU only the cache maintenance on
non-coherent systems changes: buffers are cleaned as well as invalidated.
Tested on the iPad 6: association, DHCP and SSH work, with no DART faults.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
index 069ba7016..ecf964a3e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
@@ -1638,8 +1638,9 @@ int brcmf_proto_msgbuf_attach(struct brcmf_pub *drvr)
 						     DMA_TO_DEVICE);
 	if (!msgbuf->tx_pktids)
 		goto fail;
+	/* Some firmware reads posted RX buffers, e.g. BCM4355C1 during association. */
 	msgbuf->rx_pktids = brcmf_msgbuf_init_pktids(NR_RX_PKTIDS,
-						     DMA_FROM_DEVICE);
+						     DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
 	if (!msgbuf->rx_pktids)
 		goto fail;
 
